232 0 obj
  << /ActualText (When AI speaks in clean lines\054 we assume it knows more than it does\056 But ambiguity in strategy isn\031t always about lack of data\054 sometimes it\031s about irreducible complexity\056\n\nThis principle is about\240calibrating how that complexity shows up\056\nExplicit uncertainty\240builds\240trust through transparency\054 showing where the limits are\056\nInferential uncertainty\240feels more\240naturalistic\054 mirroring how human advisors hedge \024 and inviting interpretation\056\n\nThis is a tension between\240rational trust calibration and intuitive ambiguity sensing\056\n\nExecutives toggling between analysis and instinct may prefer one mode over the other depending on the stakes\054 the audience\054 or the style of decision\055making culture they\031re in\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 233 0 R
     /Pg 226 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
